# Local research artifact; its content lives in specs/.
# The leading slash is required: unanchored, and with core.ignorecase=true, this
# pattern also matches specs/design.md.
/DESIGN.md

# Working plans. Provenance, not product.
plans/

# Local agent/editor tooling. specs/ is the source of truth for this project.
.claude/

# Job artifacts. Container stdout is streamed to logs/<JOB_ID>.log and job dirs
# hold a clone plus the /job inputs. Both contain agent output driven by untrusted
# issue text, and a job dir transiently holds a scoped GITHUB_TOKEN's working tree.
# Never commit either.
logs/
jobs/

# Persisted agent session transcripts (PI_SESSIONS_DIR, REQ-RESUMABLE-SESSION). Strictly MORE
# PII-bearing than logs/: a transcript holds the issue text, the file contents the agent read, its
# tool output and its own reasoning -- and unlike the raw job log it has to exist for resume to work
# at all. The default is no default: PI_SESSIONS_DIR is unset until an operator picks a path, so these
# two patterns catch the conventional layout (a sessions/ dir here) and the exact filename the store
# writes. A bare *.jsonl was considered and rejected: it would also silently swallow a future test
# fixture, and a pattern that makes `git add` do nothing is its own trap. An operator who puts
# PI_SESSIONS_DIR somewhere else inside a repo is covered by `pi-dispatch doctor`, which warns with the
# path. Never commit either.
sessions/
current.jsonl

# The GitHub App private key. `pi-dispatch setup github` writes github-app-<slug>.pem into the
# deployment folder itself (worker/src/github-app-setup.mjs) at mode 0600, and when that folder is a
# checkout of this repo the key lands right here -- where 0600 stops meaning anything the moment
# `git add -A` stages it. Broad rather than github-app-*.pem on purpose: an operator who renamed the
# key, or brought their own, made the same mistake and deserves the same net. This is deliberately NOT
# the `*.jsonl` case argued against above: nothing matching *.pem is tracked, the tests that need a key
# mint one into a temp dir, and if a fixture ever needs to ship, the `!name.example.json` convention
# used throughout this file un-ignores it in one line. `pi-dispatch doctor` covers a key kept outside
# this repo, warning when it sits in a work tree that does not ignore it.
*.pem

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
coverage/
*.tgz
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Unified trigger list. Holds host paths and per-trigger tasks; the committed
# triggers.example.json is the template, and deploy/triggers.json is the deployed default.
/triggers.json
!triggers.example.json

# Scoped pause windows ("quiet hours"). pause-windows.example.json is the template to copy windows out
# of; the EMPTY one an operator actually runs is scaffolded into the deployment folder by `pi-dispatch
# init` (worker/src/init.mjs), which is why the scaffold is committable by accident without this rule.
# There is no copy under deploy/: the worker resolves this file only via PI_PAUSE_WINDOWS_FILE, so one
# sitting among the service templates would be read by nothing. See docs/pause-windows.md.
/pause-windows.json
!pause-windows.example.json

# Pinned third-party pi packages (issue #58). init scaffolds pi-packages.json into the
# cwd, so without this rule the scaffold is committable by accident; the committed
# pi-packages.example.json is the template.
/pi-packages.json
!pi-packages.example.json

# Operator-declared subscription plans (issue #53). Prices only — counterfactual cost
# analytics for the admin, never job behavior; subscriptions.example.json is the template.
/subscriptions.json
!subscriptions.example.json

# Python — bytecode and tool caches from the skill scripts under .claude/skills/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/

# Editors and OS. This is a public repo with contributors on other platforms.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
